text:
Arjun: Quick check-in — eng + product + infra: we need a concrete ingest contract for the per-1k-token cost rollup and cache/batch savings. Who owns the runtime signals? I'm proposing fields: model_id, model_variant, tokens_in, tokens_out, kv_cache_hit_tokens, batch_group_size, gpu_seconds, node_type. Thoughts?

Mei: +1. Runtime team can emit tokens_in/out and kv cache hits. Need to standardize names. Suggest: tokens_req, tokens_resp, kv_hit_tokens, kv_miss_tokens, batch_size. Also add routing_policy tag (e.g., prefer_low_cost / sla_high).

Tom: We can emit per-request proto, but watch cardinality. node_type and region ok, but model_variant should be coarse (quantized_int8 / fp16 / float32) not commit hash.

Priya: Console needs pre-aggregated 1m rollups and per-route cost attribution. We want cost_per_1k = (gpu_seconds * gpu_cost_per_sec + infra_costs) / (tokens_resp/1000). Doable?

Lucia: Finance needs sample numbers from staging for avg batch sizes to validate unit cost. Also we need mapping to billing SKU and product tags.

deploy-bot: New collector v2 deployed to staging at 16:12 :rocket:

Mei: Proposed minimal schema attached — paste:
```
message TokenCostEvent {
  string model_id = 1;
  string model_tier = 2; // e.g., quantized_int8 / fp16
  int64 tokens_req = 3;
  int64 tokens_resp = 4;
  int64 kv_hit_tokens = 5;
  int64 kv_miss_tokens = 6;
  int32 batch_size = 7;
  double gpu_seconds = 8;
  string routing_reason = 9; // prefer_low_cost | sla_strict | fallback
  string region = 10;
}
```

Arjun: Two open Qs — 1) who owns rollout flags for routing to cheaper variants? 2) How to annotate fallbacks so savings aren't double-counted?

Tom: Runtime will set routing_reason and emit original_model_id + served_model_id for fallbacks. That should make attribution deterministic.

Priya: For console UX, we want split: top-level cost.total_per_1k and a drilldown showing savings.cache_per_1k vs savings.batch_per_1k vs savings.quant_per_1k. Metric names must be consistent across infra/monitoring.

Lucia: Approve metric names. Also request a sample CSV from staging exports for validation.

Arjun: Action items — Tom: add tags + proto to collector (ETA Thu). Mei: add 1m rollup job + schema to ingest repo (ETA Fri). Priya: wire metrics + mock console GIF (ETA next Wed). I'll file tickets after this thread.

Mei: Quick Q — raw token-level events or only pre-aggregated windows? Raw gives flexibility but high volume.

Tom: We'll emit sampled raw events + mandatory 1m aggregates to balance fidelity and cost.

Priya: Great — I'll coordinate with @analytics and product to include these fields in the dashboard template.

Arjun: :thumbsup: If no blockers, mark ready for implementation in tomorrow sync.
